// The window device's clicks in a row, the secondary button, the keys
// shortcuts are made with, the pointer's shape, a menu at the pointer,
// the menu bar, a folder chosen and an alert,
// through the headless device: nothing pressed, no menu chosen (-1).
// (The menus themselves need a window: a Mac's and the drawn one were
// tried by hand.)
// RUN: sh %S/Inputs/headless.sh %t.dir
// RUN: %ent run -I %t.dir %S/Inputs/window_menu.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      clicks 0 secondary false command false word false
// CHECK-NEXT: name Ctrl
// CHECK-NEXT: menu -1 shapes 2 4 5
// CHECK-NEXT: bar false chosen [] folder [] alert -1
